<title>UK: Glaxo shares slip after broker downgrade.</title>
<headline>Glaxo shares slip after broker downgrade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in pharmaceutical giant Glaxo Wellcome fell in early trading Wednesday after Lehman Brothers downgraded the stock to &quot;hold&quot; from &quot;outperform&quot;, market sources said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a value call, earnings estimates haven't been changed,&quot; said one.</p>
<p>Shares in Glaxo eased 11p to 10.10 stg.</p>
<p>Lehman analysts were not immediately available to comment.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8712</p>
</text>
